2. WHY (quoted; the drafts it rests on are unchecked)
   W138's new failure mode (l4reg_compare.out section 4 (7)): "the limiter's latent loss of its limit (HO-D, L4A-58: FAULT asserts only while limiting)"
   SLVS841F 9.3.3 (page 14, DESCRIBED): "The FAULT open-drain output is asserted (active low) during an overcurrent, overtemperature, or reverse-voltage condition."; and: "The TPS255x-1 asserts the FAULT signal during a fault condition and remains asserted while the part is latched-off. The FAULT signal is de-asserted once device power is cycled or the enable is toggled"
   the ledger's HO-D (REMAINING-ENGINEERING.md): "Unresolved. A diagnostic with a bounded interval covering faults after start-up and in the diagnostic itself"
   the guard's objection (L8P-BREAKER.md, finding L8P-R9-F1): "No automatic diagnostic is drafted: one that tests a shunt opens
     the breaker in service": here the quorum tolerates one supervisor out (IOHA row 3: "the other two are a majority and
     ownership is unaffected"), so a test that switches its target off is admissible
   the owner's part 24: "Any automatic diagnostic needs a bounded detection/response interval, including faults that arise after startup and faults affecting the diagnostic itself."
   the register's row (inputs/l4ai-register-L4A-58-row.tsv, sha256 c4084ad2, copied from the coordinator's _runs/l4ai/register.tsv): L4A-58 HO-D under the limiter: a peer-run in-service test of each supervisor's limiter ...

