     reset or dark leaves its pin analog (RM0433 p.533) and the gate at most 0.0350 V (the pin's 250 nA and IGSS 100 nA into 100
     kOhm) against VGS(th) 0.65 V
   FAULT low at a peer's pin: VOL 0.18 V at 1 mA (PRINTED; it sinks at most 0.707 mA from the two pull-ups) plus the BAT46W's
     VF 0.45 V at 10 mA (PRINTED, 25 C) and 0.10 V for the cold (ASSUMPTION): at most 0.730 V against 0.3 VDD = 0.9727 V (Table
     157)
   FAULT high at a peer's pin: its own rail through 10 kOhm less the pin's 250 nA, the other (dark) peer's diode reverse
     current 20 uA (ASSUMPTION at 76.25 C: 5 uA at 60 C and 1.5 V PRINTED) and FAULT's 1 uA off-state leakage (PRINTED): at least
     3.0191 V against 0.7 VDD = 2.3504 V; no pin ever sees more than its own rail; a dark peer's anode sits at its dark rail, its
     diode reverse biased
   each ADC pin: at most 2.7491 V (the output's top 4.1174 V on the divider's highest ratio), inside 0 to VREF+ (Table 184,
     VREF+ the peer's own rail, at least 3.2422 V) and under the FT pins' 4.0 V unpowered (FT_xxx: Min(VDD, ...) + 4.0 V, so 4.0
     V unpowered); a shorted divider top puts the output on the pin, 4.1174 V at most: inside an FT pin's limit while powered
     (VDD + 3.6 V, Table 157 note 6), 0.1174 V over 4.0 V only while that peer is dark (a residual of the double condition,
     W146-F9)
   the loads the path adds: the two dividers 0.277 mA on each limiter's output; a peer's rail carries its two FAULT pull-ups
     only while FAULT is low (0.353 mA); the gates draw nothing static: no case row changes (a labelled scenario for the
     coordinator, W146-F6)
   the tested target's regulator while the load conducts: the load's bottom at most 0.0785 V (IOSmax through both switches hot,
     INFERRED), its EN through the BAT46W at most 0.4285 V (VF 0.25 V at 0.1 mA PRINTED, it carries 18 uA from the EN's 100 kOhm,
     and 0.10 V for the cold, ASSUMPTION) against the TPS737's 0.5 V low (SBVS067W 5.6, PRINTED): the regulator is off and blocks
     reverse current (6.3.4, DESCRIBED); with either half open the load carries nothing, its bottom sits at the output and the
     diode is off; with the limit lost the bottom rises to the lost current's drop and the test aborts anyway
   the second barrier: while its limiter limits the output is 1.288 to 1.792 V, so the target's rail is under VBOR2's 2.25 V
     falling minimum (PRINTED) and with BOR at level 2 (DRAFTED, W146-D9) it is held in reset even with the EN diode open
   all levels hold: yes

8. THE TEST'S ELECTRICAL ACCEPTANCE (the judge; MODEL on PRINTED; ASSUMPTION and DRAFTED figures named)
   the reading (each peer, its own): I = V / 3.0 Ohm from the output's mean 1 to 4 ms after the drop, the pin's voltage taken against the peer's own
     3.3 V as 3.3 V; its error terms over every corner: R_T 2.8602 to 3.1417 Ohm (1 %, 200 ppm/C over 51 K PRINTED, the load life's +-(1 % + 0.05 Ohm) as ageing,
     ASSUMPTION past 1,000 h); the divider 0.66565 to 0.66768 (0.1 %, 25 ppm/C); the rail 3.2422 to 3.3577 V (record l4canen's envelope); the ADC +-10 mV at the pin
     (ASSUMPTION: Table 186's TYPICAL +10/-20 LSB at 16 bits, no maximum printed, characterised on BGA); what the output feeds besides the load, B, 0 to
     0.5 mA: the two dividers and the regulator's EN pull-up at the output's top (MODEL on the drawn resistors) and the regulator held off by the
     EN diode (ASSUMPTION 0.3 mA: ISHDN 20 nA TYPICAL only); with that diode open, the target held in reset by BOR level 2 (its rail under the
     output, at most 1.7919 V, under VBOR2's 2.25 V falling minimum, PRINTED), B at most 20 mA (ASSUMPTION): the second barrier
   record l9t5's supply path at board B (W138's reading of it): the least input 3.7579 V less 0.04252 Ohm times the lead's current; the served peak
     S3' 0.4240 A a supervisor (record l4reg's section 2)
   the acceptance: a healthy limiter (0.4702 to 0.5704 A) reads 0.4345 to 0.6140 A over every corner: PASS inside, LIMIT LOW under, LIMIT HIGH over (DRAFTED)
