      is at least 3.3911 V (the least input less the lost current 1.4396 A and the target's 0.4240 A through the limiter's 0.135
      Ohm) and reads at least 3.3130 V; the abort at 2.5 V lies between them over every corner of the reading
   J6 holds each half alone for 4.0 ms, under the least deglitch 5.0 ms (PRINTED): a stuck other half loads the rail for at
      most that and nothing latches
   J7 holds the reading 1.0 to 4.0 ms after the drop each peer sees, before the least deglitch 5.0 ms; its start 1 ms after
      the drop is 500 times the TYPICAL 2 us response (ASSUMPTION that the limit has settled)
   J8 holds the limiter dissipates at most 15.8 mJ in a test (its drop at most 2.7739 V at IOSmax for the 10 ms deglitch),
      inside W138's 23.5 mJ latch case (an output short)
   J9 holds the gates at least 2.8141 V (VOH at -8 mA, 1 kOhm and 100 kOhm); the upper switch's VGS at least 2.7150 V with
      1.4396 A in the lower: over the 2.5 V RDS(on) row; 1.4396 A against ID 4.7 A at 70 C
   the judge: HOLDS
     mutated, a TYPICAL deglitch (7.5 ms) taken as the bound:                                        FAILS (J0)
     mutated, a test that cannot detect a lost limit: R_T 10 Ohm (a healthy limiter never limits):   FAILS (J1, J5)
     mutated, R_T 1.0 Ohm (a lost limit's current over U601):                                        FAILS (J2, J3)
     mutated, each half alone for 6 ms (a stuck other half latches the target):                      FAILS (J6)
     mutated, the reading to 5.5 ms after the drop (past the least deglitch):                        FAILS (J7)

9. THE PROCEDURE (DRAFTED for Layer 5's contract; L4A-61 propagates it) AND ITS TIMING on the printed figures
   preconditions, each peer on its own observation: all three in the quorum on both fabrics for the last 10 windows, no other HO-D test and no
   contained node, the target's FAULT high and its output in band; the schedule (DRAFTED, W146-D5): the first round 60 s after the quorum first
   holds (A, B, C 20 s apart), then each supervisor every 3600 s, the three 1200 s apart; a test whose preconditions fail waits for the next window
   step 0, the announcement (0.100 s): both peers mark the target under test in their state frames (one window); from here
      canen's automatic restart and FW-B21's stop do not act on it and the self-test's phases skip by their own precondition
      (all three functional)
   step 1, the restore route exercised (2.190 s): both peers assert their restart votes (record l4canen's route); each sees
      the output under 2.0 V within 1.384 s (the gate over 2.5 V 1.208 s, the limiter's turn-off 3 ms PRINTED, the node and the
      target's domain (16 uF, ASSUMPTION) on the two dividers alone), releases, and sees it back over 3.3 V within 0.804 s (the
      gate under its threshold 0.799 s, ton 3 ms and tr 1.5 ms PRINTED); else ABORT, nothing latched
   step 1s, settle (0.020 s): the output at 3.3 V or more for 20 ms (the target restarting under its limiter)
   step 2, each half alone (0.012 s): the next controller closes the upper half for 4 ms, then, 6 ms later by its own clock,
      the one after closes the lower half for 4 ms; both read the output: a drop under 2.5 V is the OTHER half stuck on (SWITCH
      STUCK ON); under the 5 ms least deglitch, so nothing latches
   step 3, the load (0.019 s): the upper half closes, then the lower (the load's moment, its closer's clock); the closer
      checks the output under 2.5 V 0.2 ms after closing, the other peer 3.2 ms after its own, else opens at once (LIMIT NOT
      SHOWN); each reads the output 1 to 4 ms after the drop it sees (I = V / 3.0 Ohm), FAULT's fall 4.75 to 10.25 ms after it,
      the output under 0.3 V 1 ms after FAULT (latched); both open 12 ms after the drop at the latest; the output stays under
      0.3 V for 5 ms with the load open (LATCHED)
   step 4, the restore (3.604 s): both peers assert their restart votes for 2.0 s (canen's hold), release; the gate under its
      threshold 0.799 s, ton 3 ms and tr 1.5 ms PRINTED, the output back over 3.3 V and FAULT high (9.3.3: 'de-asserted once ...
      the enable is toggled'); the target boots and rejoins within 0.800 s (W139: boot 0.5 s ASSUMPTION, 2 windows listening,
      its slot)
   any failed check: both peers open their halves, the verdict goes into their state frames and the kit's status path, the target is restored
     if latched (step 4) or simply readmitted if never latched; that supervisor's tests stop until the next start (DRAFTED, W146-D6); each peer
     writes the target and the step to its backup registers before step 3 and clears it after step 4, so a peer that boots with a step 3
     recorded (the survivors reset by the step's transient, W146-F10) takes that test as failed (LIMIT NOT SHOWN) and stops its tests: the
     transient cannot repeat on every restart (DRAFTED; the registers' retention through a brown-out reset is RM0433's backup domain, not
     read here: ASSUMPTION; DS12110 describes VBAT supplying that domain when VDD is absent)
   THE INTERVAL THE TARGET IS OUT of the quorum: 5.945 s (the announcement 0.1 s, step 1 2.190 s, settle 0.020 s, step 2 0.012 s, step 3 0.019 s, step 4 3.604 s)
     (MODEL on PRINTED, DRAFTED and the boot and domain ASSUMPTIONs; record l4canen's recovery 5.603 s is step 4 plus its 2.0 s decision)
   THE SERVICE LOST: two of three serve for that interval (IOHA row 3: ownership unaffected); the quorum has no spare then (a
     second supervisor out is row 4's home assignment); 0.50 % of the time at 3600 s a supervisor. The survivors keep their
     supply on the DC path (J2 and record l4reg's J4 (c)); the transient dip of +5V_IOC at the test's load step (at most 0.5704
     A with a healthy limit, 1.4396 A with the limit lost, for the closer's 0.2 ms) is NOT bounded on printed figures (U601's
     load-transient response and the lead's inductance are not printed; the base design's own overload step of up to IOSmax has
     the same open term, W138's J7 being a DC row): PROVISIONAL, finding W146-F10. The hold-up it would need (MODEL on the
     drawn capacitors and the printed thresholds): board B's +5V_IOC carries 10.3 uF (C900, C940, C950, C960); from 3.7039 V
     before the step to the survivors' need 3.5127 V at their limiter's input it carries the lost limit's step 1.37 us, the
     healthy step 3.45 us; each survivor's own 12.0 uF (B's: C421, C422, C423, C424, C425, C426, C432, C433, C953, C954, C955,
     C956) then holds its rail from the regulator's least 3.2505 V over VBOR2's highest falling 2.37 V (PRINTED) for 24.9 us at
     its 0.4240 A peak: the survivors stay out of reset if U601 and the lead carry the step within 26.3 us (12 of U601's
     switching periods at its printed least 450 kHz); its load-transient response is printed only as TYPICAL figures, so that
     time is the supplier's pass limit (L4HOD.md section 11, task 2). Their frames hold: the target's transceivers go to the
     protected mode (bus high impedance) as its rail falls under UV(VCC) 1.65 to 2.50 V (PRINTED), its TXDs rest recessive on
     canmb's pull-ups, and W139's row R3 (a controller dark, its onset scanned over the window) reads 'a node out and
     contained' with the survivors' gap 0 windows against the loss count 3: W139's loss count respected; the target itself is
     lost to the quorum by that count, as planned, and rejoins listening first (W139-D9)
   W143's self-test skips its phases while the target is out (its own precondition: all three functional): a latent vote-path fault arising in a
     test is found within 2.60 s + 5.945 s = 8.545 s (finding W146-F2)
   THE DETECTION INTERVAL of a lost limit (MODEL on the drafted schedule and the printed timing): a limit lost after start-up is found within
     3600 s + 2.341 s = 3602.341 s of its onset (the period plus the test's verdict, steps 0 to 3); one present at start-up within 102.341 s of the quorum
     first holding; a test whose preconditions fail waits, so the interval is bounded while the preconditions hold (a node out or a fabric down
     adds its own repair time, IOHA rows 3 and 7)

